### Billing API demo walkthrough
### Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/Billing.Api --urls http://localhost:5000
### Run each request in order with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or Visual Studio / Rider (.http support).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Create a draft invoice (copy the "id" from the response into @invoiceId below)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "stadium-north", "currency": "gbp" }

###
@invoiceId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 3. Add a line: 2 x 500.00 + 20% VAT = 1,200.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Corporate box", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 500.00, "taxRate": 0.20 }

### 4. Issue it (no more edits allowed after this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/issue

### 5. Record a partial payment -> status PartiallyPaid, outstanding 700.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 500.00 }

### 6. Try to overpay -> 422 invoice.overpayment (business rule)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1000.00 }

### 7. Try to edit an issued invoice -> 422 invoice.not_draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Late extra", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10, "taxRate": 0 }

### 8. Unsupported currency -> 400 invoice.unsupported_currency (validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "stadium-north", "currency": "123" }

### 9. Unknown invoice -> 404 invoice.not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 10. Pay the rest -> status Paid, outstanding 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 700.00 }

### 11. List all invoices
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
